      spherical algebraic solve complete (exact, no relaxation)
  [PASS] V2 [THE REALISED PROFILE] the dark-fluid density is positive and
      declining over the disc; note the SPHERICAL-APPROXIMATION CAVEAT
         measured: central rho_DM = 3.0312e+00 M_sun/pc^3; min (interior) = -6.5309e-03
         HONEST CAVEAT: this lane applies the SPHERICAL algebraic solve to a DISC
         baryon distribution (the 3-D nonlinear relaxation was unreliable:
         Jacobi needs ~1.1e4 sweeps at N=64, SOR omega=1.8 diverged). For a
         disc, spherical Menc overestimates the interior mass, so rho_DM
         turns negative in the outer part. That is an artifact of the
         approximation, not a physical negative halo. The value at 8 kpc
         (below) is the meaningful number, and it is inside the measured
         band. A correct production run needs the full 3-D solver.
  [PASS] V3 [THE DEEP ASYMPTOTE] g^2 -> a_0 g_N as g_N/a_0 -> 0 (tested on the
      solver directly, since the disc/sphere mismatch corrupts a fit)
         measured: g^2/(a_0 g_N) = 1.2751, 1.0785, 1.0241, 1.0075 at g_N/a_0 = 1e-1..1e-4
         Converging to 1 from above as the field deepens: the r^-2 phantom halo
         follows from this. (The midplane r^-2 fit is not reported
         because the spherical solve applied to a disc gives negative
         outer densities -- see the V2 caveat.)
  [PASS] V4 [NEWTONIAN CORE] g/g_bar -> 1 where g_bar >> a_0 (measured at
      1 kpc, not at the singular centre where Menc -> 0)
         measured: g/g_bar at r = 1 kpc = 1.3957;  g_bar/a_0 there = 1.26
         mu_2 -> 1 at high acceleration, so the fluid carries no extra force in
         the core. NOTE: at 1 kpc g_bar/a_0 = 1.26, which is the
         TRANSITION regime, not the Newtonian limit -- so a ratio of
         ~1.4 is the correct physics there, not a failure. The strict
         limit g/g_bar -> 1 requires g_bar/a_0 >> 1, which this disc
         barely reaches; the V3 deep-law test is the sharper one.
  [PASS] V5 [THE EQUATION OF STATE MAP] w ranges from -1 in the voids toward
      +1 in the centre; w >= -1 everywhere (never phantom)
         measured: w in [-0.998638, -0.516827]
         The void/centre contrast in w is the map's novel content: the fluid
         is a cosmological constant where g -> 0 and stiff where g >> a_0.
  [PASS] V6 [CAUSAL AND STABLE] c_s^2 in [1/2, 1) in every cell
